    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτύ̆χ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>misfortune, miscarriage,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				3.4.5
			</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Timocl.
				6.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fault of ignorance, mistake,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				23.70
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδίκημα, ἁμάρτημα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gorg.
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1374b6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EN</u>
				1135b12
			</span></i>: euphem., <i>crime,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρὸς τὸ δημόσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					10.20
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.14.2
			</span></i>.</div>
